==============================================================================
H046 -- IS n = 2 FORCED BY HEALTH?   (c_s^2 = mu / (mu + u mu'))
==============================================================================

==============================================================================
PART 0 -- THE FUNCTION AND THE SOUND SPEED
==============================================================================
  [PASS] A1 [THE FUNCTION] f'(K) = mu_2(sqrt K) with mu_2(u) = u(2+u)/(1+u)^2 = 1 - (1+u)^-2, exactly
         measured : f'(u^2) - mu_2(u) = 0
         threshold: symbolic difference == 0
         The kernel is a single function; the '2' in u(2+u) and the exponent
                  in (1+u)^-2 are the SAME parameter.
  [PASS] A2 [SOUND SPEED] c_s^2 = f'/(f' + 2K f'') = (u^2+3u+2)/(u^2+3u+4) = 1 - 2/(u^2+3u+4)
         measured : difference = 0
         threshold: symbolic difference == 0
         Reproduces H001/H007 independently. Note the denominator minus the
                  numerator is the CONSTANT 2 -- the same integer again.

==============================================================================
PART 1 -- HEALTH <=> mu > 0 AND mu' >= 0  (a condition on the LOG-SLOPE)
==============================================================================
  [PASS] B1 [CHAIN RULE] 2 K f''(K) = u mu'(u)  (verified on the concrete f)
         measured : 2K f'' - u mu'(u) = 0
         threshold: symbolic difference == 0
         This is the whole reason health cannot see n: c_s^2 depends on
                  mu'/mu, i.e. on the LOG-SLOPE, never on the normalisation n.
  [PASS] B2 [MASTER IDENTITY] c_s^2 = 1 / (1 + dln(mu)/dln(u))  -- health is a statement about the LOG-SLOPE only
         measured : c_s^2 - 1/(1+dlnmu/dlnu) = 0
         threshold: symbolic difference == 0
         CONSEQUENCE: c_s^2 <= 1  <=>  dln mu/dln u >= 0  <=>  mu' >= 0,
                  with no appearance of the amplitude n anywhere.
  [PASS] C1 [NO SUPERLUMINALITY] 0 <= c_s^2 <= 1 for the actual f on u in [1e-8, 1e8]
         measured : c_s^2 in [0.500000003750, 1.000000000000]
         threshold: 0 <= min and max <= 1
         The actual f is healthy. That is necessary but NOT sufficient to
                  single it out -- see Part 3.
  [PASS] C2 [NO GHOST] f'(K) = mu_2 > 0 on the same grid
         measured : min f' = 2.000000e-08
         threshold: min f' > 0
  [PASS] C3 [CONVEXITY = SUBLUMINALITY] f''(K) > 0 on the same grid
         measured : min f'' = 1.000000e-32
         threshold: min f'' > 0
         f'' > 0 is the same statement as c_s^2 < 1 (Part 1, B2).

==============================================================================
PART 2 -- WHAT (iv) DOES FORCE:  THE UNIVERSAL DEEP SOUND SPEED 1/2
==============================================================================
      mu ~ A u^q  ->  c_s^2 = 1/(q + 1)
        q = 1 : c_s^2 = 1/2
        q = 2 : c_s^2 = 1/3
        q = 3 : c_s^2 = 1/4
  [PASS] D1 [UNIVERSALITY] for mu ~ A u^q the sound speed is exactly 1/(1+q), independent of the amplitude A
         measured : c_s^2(q=1,2,3) = ['1/2', '1/3', '1/4']
         threshold: c_s^2 = 1/(1+q) exactly for q = 1, 2, 3
         The amplitude A -- which is what n is -- cancels identically.
  [PASS] D2 [THE FORCED VALUE] (iv) (deep slope finite and non-zero) means q = 1, hence c_s^2(0) = 1/2 for EVERY n
         measured : lim_K->0 c_s^2 = 1/2
         threshold: c_s^2(0) == 1/2 exactly
         THIS IS A GENUINE FORCED PREDICTION: any healthy k-essence with a
                  linear MOND regime has deep sound speed exactly c/sqrt(2).
                  The programme's measured range [1/2, 1) (H001 A-checks, H002)
                  is thus a prediction of health+(iv), not a fitted input --
                  and it holds for n = 1, 2, 3 alike, so it cannot select n.
  [PASS] D3 [MEASURED] the actual f approaches 1/2 at the deep end (the approach is linear in u: c_s^2 = 1/2 + 3u/8 + O(u^2))
         measured : c_s^2(1e-8) - 1/2 = 3.750000e-09 (predicted 3u/8 = 3.750000e-09)
         threshold: |c_s^2(1e-8) - 1/2| < 1e-8 and the deviation equals 3u/8 to 1e-12

==============================================================================
